+- **#2285 (probe lane-2 blindness)** fixed the probe's ability to *find* branch heads for stranded WOs (OPEN_REPO first, `bridge/<taskId>` head, cap-tolerant layer-2 scan). It is a detection repair; it does not itself re-stamp. Its "un-sticks 15 stranded WOs" framing names the queued-label cohort (pattern-1 class), not the rejected-label cohort.
+- **#2293 (R58 sweep)** executed #2275's claim and produced the deterministic 52-row rejected-plane worklist — an enumeration advance (the sweep found the plane 52 rows deep where the strict plane saw 20), but the sweep's landing is report/tracker material; the re-stamp action itself remains routed to the tower-owner plane (R58 option A), which is HITL-gated.
+- **#2347 (limit ladder)** closed the fetch-limit gap #2293 surfaced (`_fetch_rejected_rows_tower` sent no limit). Again enumeration-plane; no verdict writes.
+- Net: the detection and enumeration planes are now fully green, and the *action* plane — the tower-owner adjudication sweep that re-stamps `bridge:rejected` → terminal-correct — is the sole remaining step, unchanged since R58 was filed (~21:0xZ 10-28). The pattern-2 instances are the extreme end of the wait: **~18 hours from false stamp to still-unrestored, through three landed fixes and two clean sweeps.**
